### Finding G01-2 🟡 minor (IN-16, real but ungraded)
Evidence environment/data/override_precedence.conf: "match_version = effective version from policy_version_map". Each override row carries its own `version` and its window in effective_windows.xml carries another `version`; the rule does not say which one must equal the effective version. tests/test_output.py reference_documents requires both (window version and row version == v100), solution/solve.py checks only `window["version"] != version`, TRUTH.md:22 says "window version equal to the effective version". 40 rows have row version != window version (e.g. t-atlas OV-F195 v195 in WIN-F015 v015), but none of them sits in a window containing the effective instant in the shipped corpus or the hidden heads, so no graded outcome differs today.
