## Lessons for the master
1. Mutation testing beats reading for AL-27: about 60 one-rule mutants of solve.py run through the bundle's own tests found three untriggered rules in minutes.
2. Re-run the previous round's AL-27 list as mutants too; two v4 rules (zero denominator, missing manifest record) survived and my fresh mutant list missed them.
3. Variant-spelling generators that touch only row 0 of a shuffled table give no guarantee the variant reaches a graded figure; pin variants to rows that do.
4. "Not tested when X fails" rules need a fixture for every reason they gate, not just one.
5. A declared deviation in TRUTH.md (TS-29 floats) is not a kit waiver; it needs the tasker's sign-off or a code change.
